{"title":"2015 AIME I Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Hint\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Hint</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Potential_Inspiration\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Potential Inspiration</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(NOT_RIGOROUS)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(NOT RIGOROUS)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(short)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (short)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Generalization\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Generalization</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_solution_by_Claire_Wang_(using_hockey_stick_identity)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video solution by Claire Wang (using hockey stick identity)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider all 1000-element subsets of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4ddee8257c92f75a66573edb42b93e1997c67d04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, ... , 2015\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />.  From each such subset choose the least element.  The arithmetic mean of all of these least elements is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/4/7347a1d5586e82c832f61ea799d89945ed2837fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p}{q}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"11\" height=\"36\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/6/856ee48ce76ddbd106a05384c2ea2c28e3b76c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p + q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Hint\">Hint</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Hint\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Use the Hockey Stick Identity in the form\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/9/5995d78139aa36d79bf26ac228389406a12a6261.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{a}{a} + \\binom{a+1}{a} + \\binom{a+2}{a} + \\dots + \\binom{b}{a} = \\binom{b+1}{a+1}.\\]\" width=\"416\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>(This is best proven by a combinatorial argument that coincidentally pertains to the problem: count two ways the number of subsets of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/0/0e0f4b89661df565c69d2394ebd4f262edc10913.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(b + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" /> numbers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/b/bcb544573e4e7752e6ef4b95d6c8e953adcf558f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a + 1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" /> elements whose least element is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/7/e37df861b8576800b854551cbbe49ca711a5e0be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 \\le i \\le b - a + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"137\" height=\"17\" />.)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> be the desired mean. Then because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3fae72dc506d23b92c02760d3b931173c3dd7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{2015}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" /> subsets have 1000 elements and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb4b92107d208b62c3e2cf532fd01f3c9df8b78.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{2015 - i}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"89\" height=\"53\" /> have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> as their least element,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/e/22eab90fa0b91d86da3469ddc99c27482a9f00a8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} \\binom{2015}{1000} M &amp;= 1 \\cdot \\binom{2014}{999} + 2 \\cdot \\binom{2013}{999} + \\dots + 1016 \\cdot \\binom{999}{999} \\\\      &amp;= \\binom{2014}{999} + \\binom{2013}{999} + \\dots + \\binom{999}{999} \\\\      &amp;                      + \\binom{2013}{999} + \\binom{2012}{999} + \\dots + \\binom{999}{999} \\\\      &amp; \\dots \\\\      &amp; + \\binom{999}{999} \\\\      &amp;= \\binom{2015}{1000} + \\binom{2014}{1000} + \\dots + \\binom{1000}{1000} \\\\      &amp;= \\binom{2016}{1001}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"466\" height=\"380\" />\nUsing the definition of binomial coefficient and the identity <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/9/ee9c368e624492e4f694855d883ade0277e02ad2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n! = n \\cdot (n-1)!$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"124\" height=\"18\" />, we deduce that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/b/e1b3d7637ffbc13c55b4c821e91100ba4943e58e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[M = \\frac{2016}{1001} = \\frac{288}{143}.\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"38\" />\nThe answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/b/abbb15034deac6493b20e5735b43291f83f3a33c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{431}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"45\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Potential_Inspiration\">Potential Inspiration</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Potential Inspiration\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For solution 1, the inspiration could be that once we select the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/b/46b9f64d04014b35be5c3887fdbf220890630915.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1, a_2,...,a_{2015}\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/3/c631daa1a2a7d7a39f30aa808dbb59a34e3bb73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1&lt;a_2&lt;...&lt;a_{2015}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"161\" height=\"15\" />, we want to multiply each such set by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> and sum up through all such sets.\n</p><p>So, how do we scale each such set by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />? We realize that if we were to choose one more element, specifically, less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, this could be done in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/0/ba05a36f5b16f386b6fd1725c2af867da9d8cb92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" /> ways.\n</p><p>Oh! So, now if we add <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to all the numbers in our set, they become <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/5246f5b4647f9f03b33cf57dbf1bfc3548a2cae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1+1, a_2+1,...,a_{2015}+1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"224\" height=\"20\" />, so the number of ways to pick another number below the least number in this set is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />!\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Each 1000-element subset <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42497668ece9f1fa81523c12787cae0a4f96b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{ a_1, a_2,a_3,...,a_{1000}\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" /> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/2/952c5588d0de98bde902d89e7549145f474d0669.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{1,2,3,...,2015\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e9ab54bda62573f494b00a60c862d499c2df7b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1&lt;a_2&lt;a_3&lt;...&lt;a_{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"198\" height=\"12\" /> contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> to the sum of the least element of each subset. Now, consider the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/8/d9843b57c03a71aa1a9a8769b234c5037c419910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{a_1+1,a_2+1,a_3+1,...,a_{1000}+1\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"278\" height=\"18\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> ways to choose a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/8/828b84feac6a0146f8caccc584d507b89d3237c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;a_1+1&lt;a_2+1,a_3+1&lt;...&lt;a_{1000}+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"342\" height=\"16\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> can be anything from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> inclusive). Thus, the number of ways to choose the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86a452bc69b52a020e1b0df2ac37f1392da1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{k,a_1+1,a_2+1,a_3+1,...,a_{1000}+1\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" /> is equal to the sum. But choosing a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec86a452bc69b52a020e1b0df2ac37f1392da1e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{k,a_1+1,a_2+1,a_3+1,...,a_{1000}+1\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"296\" height=\"18\" /> is the same as choosing a 1001-element subset from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/9/b294f42825e7aaf5cad4faa5c685231824b48081.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left\\{1,2,3,...,2016\\right\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"128\" height=\"18\" />! \n</p><p>Thus, the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/5/e459aa231f66ec07f0275c172597e6719387c965.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\binom{2016}{1001}}{\\binom{2015}{1000}}=\\frac{2016}{1001}=\\frac{288}{143}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"165\" height=\"49\" />. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/4/9547d8768cd23a09e2155b7aa472bae100525257.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q=288+143=\\boxed{431}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3.28NOT_RIGOROUS.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(NOT_RIGOROUS)\">Solution 3(NOT RIGOROUS)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(NOT RIGOROUS)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the size of the large set and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be the size of the subset (i.e. in this problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb347b8310821a140983648bb9193a864113d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274b6e92ba90fa8434f94e3a4aea1a9a5293fbfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />). We can easily find the answers for smaller values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />:\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e129fbcb9c592946641c11f0c3eb03a078b4bdf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0876f5b5cc06465d4d110633cd1463412131defc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bee8bc4dabea7532e7359aa8ac83217db2f4dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0876f5b5cc06465d4d110633cd1463412131defc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab458a1f23acc24632e0d00177f2b09b29fa92d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac43$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be241415c542a527773b9c883ce3cba4c07f1d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0876f5b5cc06465d4d110633cd1463412131defc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/1/391bb8a2f1c23492a7e0d68c2dc19b6a2c027fb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac53$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5bee8bc4dabea7532e7359aa8ac83217db2f4dcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1f0e349110d5955f42484f6123e7bc09cf1c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/e/6be241415c542a527773b9c883ce3cba4c07f1d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1f0e349110d5955f42484f6123e7bc09cf1c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0af5e1b6cfb1551ce48c49f840977c850c64b248.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac54$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"11\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/4/3940bf1382392a6b1b4f106d262cb8e1223d223b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/1/7c1f0e349110d5955f42484f6123e7bc09cf1c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/d/add685ffcf9823b32ee3100dc9e8a85549e223f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>At this point, we can see a pattern: our desired answer is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717457404e6d66a0e982181820abf156c1233703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{p+1}{q+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"42\" height=\"40\" />. Plugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cb347b8310821a140983648bb9193a864113d1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p = 2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/4/274b6e92ba90fa8434f94e3a4aea1a9a5293fbfb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"68\" height=\"16\" />, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/a/f3ad181dc85745ace21be37c566cb0d2fcf5f2ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2016}{1001}=\\frac{288}{143}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/7/8b716eddfb4c1274d7e337b82de06cffeca42cbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$288 + 143 = \\boxed{431}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"140\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28short.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(short)\">Solution 4 (short)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (short)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>In the \"average case\", the numbers evenly partition the interval [0,2016] into 1001 parts. Then because it asks for the expected value of the least element the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47cac34fb79ccf0791fb8577349b51757064e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2016}{1001}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"38\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>-tigershark22\n</p><p>VIEWER NOTE: This solution doesn't always work, for example, take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/6/e861e10e1c19918756b9c8b7717684593c63aeb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[0,1]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" />. The \"average case\" is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/0/26013b9caa10ba07cc83b7f7d09884980227ad25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{1}{2}\\implies n^2=\\frac{1}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"155\" height=\"38\" /> but integrating <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/0/6006bba637eef443381fbaff768fa62d9ff41e62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> we see that definitely is not the case. This works only in certain situations, so maybe this solution would be better off with proof that this is one of those situations.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When it says average, it really just means expected value. Let's do casework.\n</p><p>Our first case is when the smallest number in the subset is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/16794ed8d576bcdfc1b48ac2155ce53ff11aff25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2014$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" /> numbers to choose from, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> numbers left to choose. So, this contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/a/44ac46f74ef68af5dd2e6f98b7e6db4ad76206d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{2014}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"66\" height=\"55\" /> to our expected value.\n</p><p>Then, for the smallest number being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/a/2fa725c98dfe19f98809033755b801810bc298aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2013$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" /> numbers to choose from and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> numbers left to choose. So, this contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/8/a28a408044b82cca84fbb8176db882f66dcea734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\dbinom{2013}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"75\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, the smallest number being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> contributes <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fcbd958796bc9ea2d551b29d7be88eab3705f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\dbinom{2012}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"75\" height=\"55\" /> to our expected value. We keep this up all the way to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/9/1e92f1fe558f26a433c46cc9ec749775a9ff901e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1016\\dbinom{999}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"94\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p><p>This makes our sum\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f917d694a576747a19ab9a6b2290e12a84e5a423.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{2014}{999} + 2\\dbinom{2013}{999} + 3\\dbinom{2012}{999} + \\cdots + 1016\\dbinom{999}{999}.\\]\" width=\"413\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>To evaluate this, we can split each binomial into groups of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, like this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/505485eb461dc619db714a12ab42f94d805a7a73.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\binom{2014}{999} + \\binom{2013}{999} + \\binom{2013}{999} + \\binom{2012}{999} + \\binom{2012}{999} + \\binom{2012}{999} + \\cdots + \\underbrace{\\binom{999}{999} + \\binom{999}{999} + \\cdots + \\binom{999}{999}}_{\\text{1016 }\\binom{999}{999}\\text{&#39;s}}.\\]\" width=\"763\" height=\"86\" />\n</p><p>Now, we can turn this into:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/e/16e6e8c33dc8e0dc379c85daeaab1ceba7c54c76.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\binom{2014}{999} + \\binom{2013}{999} + \\cdots + \\binom{999}{999} \\right) + \\left( \\binom{2013}{999} + \\binom{2012}{999} + \\cdots + \\binom{999}{999} \\right) + \\cdots + \\left( \\binom{1000}{999} + \\binom{999}{999} \\right) + \\binom{999}{999}.\\]\" width=\"903\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Now, by the Hockey Stick Identity, we can further simplify this into\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/0/70057d0758fd8e65d1c4e0d9f46cb3a9747271df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{2015}{1000} + \\dbinom{2014}{1000} + \\cdots + \\dbinom{1001}{1000} + \\dbinom{1000}{1000}.\\]\" width=\"367\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Further simplifying this, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b2568f09f82f5ec89c2d92e40d5e9420246c06.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dbinom{2016}{1001}.\\]\" width=\"64\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>If this is our sum and there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/3/cb3fae72dc506d23b92c02760d3b931173c3dd7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dbinom{2015}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"60\" height=\"53\" /> possible subsets, our average is simply\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/3/183bfcd0649c2aac0a99bb89fffb793c5d0a1551.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{\\dbinom{2016}{1001}}{\\dbinom{2015}{1000}} = \\dfrac{2016!}{1001!\\,1015!} \\times \\dfrac{1000!\\,1015!}{2015!} = \\dfrac{2016}{1001} = \\dfrac{288}{143} \\Longrightarrow \\boxed{431}.\\]\" width=\"494\" height=\"112\" />\n</p><p>-jb2015007\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By 1981 IMO P2, for a collection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> elements from an <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> element set the arithmetic mean of these smallest sets is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/e/5be9283ad317912e4d51033bf35cf5b180fda0e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n+1}{r+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"48\" height=\"40\" />. Thus, the average is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/3/af3b4959199761b1c27b809755e6d2d10ac8932e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2016}{1001} = \\frac{288}{143} \\implies \\boxed{431}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"186\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>We will also attempt to solve this traditionally.\n</p><p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/f/5ff3cfa265147804651438ce9189c9b01e28e766.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2015}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"66\" height=\"55\" /> subsets. The largest \"minimum\" element would be 1016, which appears once. The second largest would be 1015, which appears exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d32b1401ed53450f874c883582c21ac2e578d5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{2015-1015}{999} = \\binom{1000}{999}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"214\" height=\"55\" /> times. Indeed, summing over all such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, we see that the numerator is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a96790311e792be0be7043332a208bea4f8748.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{k=1}^{1016} k\\binom{2015-k}{999}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"53\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/c/c9c830e70fe2e227b5169ee706e3a45d5ad6933c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sum_{j=1}^{1016} \\sum_{k=j}^{1016} \\binom{2015-j}{999}\\]\" width=\"168\" height=\"55\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/8/ff8b8e055205fe6323a96c157d32ff82d55505d6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\sum_{j=1}^{1016} (\\binom{2016-j}{1000})\\]\" width=\"152\" height=\"54\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/f/71f8671a6a11ecbcba1ca05eb686311b995fa0ec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 2016-j, \\sum_{x=1000}^{2015} \\binom{x}{1000}\\]\" width=\"216\" height=\"53\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d837b815ad2b89cce97e6070fd9327e28ffa43b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[= \\binom{2016}{1001}\\]\" width=\"78\" height=\"53\" />.\n</p><p>So the mean is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/7/4975969b7949a25b4beee612ad5d4c4c80304f67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\binom{2016}{1001}}{\\binom{2015}{1000}} = \\frac{288}{143} \\implies \\boxed{431} \\quad \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -21px\" width=\"223\" height=\"51\" />.\n</p><p>I will make a proof for the IMO variant of this problem later.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t-yHTkGkMK4\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=t-yHTkGkMK4</a>\n~anellipticcurveoverq\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Generalization\">Generalization</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Generalization\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/1981_IMO_Problems/Problem_2</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_solution_by_Claire_Wang_.28using_hockey_stick_identity.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_solution_by_Claire_Wang_(using_hockey_stick_identity)\">Video solution by Claire Wang (using hockey stick identity)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video solution by Claire Wang (using hockey stick identity)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DijcbHaRez4\">https://youtu.be/DijcbHaRez4</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I\" title=\"2015 AIME I\">2015 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2015 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2015 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemso